**2. Competitor Profiles**

**2.1 Procore Technologies**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Attribute**    **Detail**
  ---------------- ------------------------------------------------------
  Founded / HQ     2002 / Carpinteria, CA. IPO 2021 (NYSE: PCOR). Market
                   cap \~\$11B.

  Target market    Large general contractors, ENR 400 companies, \$50M+
                   annual volume

  Pricing          \$375--\$1,200+/month --- notoriously opaque,
                   sales-required, annual contracts. Frequently
                   \$5,000--\$30,000/year for mid-size GCs.

  Core strengths   Dominant brand in enterprise GC market. Deep feature
                   set. Large partner ecosystem. Strong compliance and
                   AIA billing.

  Core weaknesses  Completely inaccessible to small/mid contractors on
                   price. No trade-specific workflows. Single-tenant
                   architecture --- no sub collaboration. Overkill for
                   most jobs.

  Trade support    Generic project management --- no native trade
                   modules. Electrical and plumbing tracked as generic
                   tasks.

  Mobile app       Solid but complex --- designed for office PMs, not
                   field workers. Known for steep learning curve.

  Market position  Dominant in enterprise (\$50M+ revenue contractors).
                   Largely absent in small/mid market.

  Our advantage vs Price (10× cheaper for SMB), trade-specific workflows,
  Procore          cross-tenant collaboration, mobile field-first design,
                   faster onboarding
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**2.2 Buildertrend**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Attribute**    **Detail**
  ---------------- ------------------------------------------------------
  Founded / HQ     2006 / Omaha, NE. Acquired by TZP Group (PE) 2021.

  Target market    Residential homebuilders, remodelers, custom home GCs

  Pricing          \$99--\$599/month (3 tiers). More accessible than
                   Procore.

  Core strengths   Strong residential GC workflow. Good client portal and
                   selections. Lead management built in. Reasonable
                   pricing.

  Core weaknesses  Residential-only --- limited commercial functionality.
                   No trade-specific modules. No sub collaboration
                   architecture. No electrical/plumbing/mechanical depth.
                   Poor for commercial TI or multi-trade projects.

  Trade support    None --- generic task management only. Does not
                   understand trade phases, inspection types, or
                   trade-specific data.

  Mobile app       Functional but feature-limited. Not optimized for
                   field workers.

  Market position  Strong in residential remodel/custom home market.
                   Declining relevance as projects get more complex.

  Our advantage vs Commercial capability, trade modules, cross-tenant
  Buildertrend     architecture, stronger financial workflows, better
                   mobile field experience
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**2.3 CoConstruct (now Buildertrend)**

CoConstruct merged with Buildertrend in 2021. Previously focused on
custom homebuilders with strong client communication tools. The merged
platform has not significantly addressed commercial or trade contractor
needs. Considered the same competitive profile as Buildertrend above.

**2.4 eSUB Construction Software**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Attribute**    **Detail**
  ---------------- ------------------------------------------------------
  Founded / HQ     2012 / San Diego, CA. PE-backed.

  Target market    Trade subcontractors --- electrical, mechanical,
                   plumbing, specialty. The only major platform
                   explicitly targeting subs.

  Pricing          \~\$150--\$500/month. Pricing not fully public ---
                   quote-required for larger teams.

  Core strengths   Purpose-built for trade contractors. Strong field
                   management, T&M billing, and sub-side workflow. Good
                   mobile app. Understands trade-specific operations.

  Core weaknesses  Subs only --- no GC module or GC collaboration. Cannot
                   manage projects as a prime. No client portal. Does not
                   handle GC-sub data exchange. No cross-tenant
                   architecture.

  Trade support    Good for electrical and mechanical. Limited breadth
                   --- not all trades covered equally.

  Mobile app       Strong field focus --- clock-in/out, daily reports,
                   T&M documentation.

  Market position  Niche leader for trade subs. Significant product gap:
                   subs who grow into prime roles outgrow eSUB.

  Our advantage vs GC module + prime capability, cross-tenant
  eSUB             collaboration (both sides of the GC-sub relationship),
                   client portal, broader trade coverage, better
                   financial workflows
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

