**7. Sales Battle Cards**

**7.1 When Competing Against Procore**

Prospect profile: Mid-size GC being pushed toward Procore by a large
client or GC. Sticker shock on pricing. Needs enterprise features but
can\'t justify enterprise cost.

-   Lead with price --- ask them what Procore quoted. Then show our
    Professional tier at \$349/month.

-   Ask if their subs use the platform or just get \'invited\' ---
    reveal that sub collaboration on Procore is one-sided. Subs have no
    independent environment.

-   Procore requires months of onboarding and professional services. We
    get them running in a week.

-   Procore doesn\'t understand trade workflows --- electrical circuits,
    panel schedules, plumbing pressure tests are managed as generic
    tasks. We built native modules.

-   When asked about features we lack (AIA billing, certified payroll):
    be honest --- \'That\'s coming in Q3. Here\'s what we have now that
    Procore doesn\'t: \[cross-tenant, trade modules, pricing\].

**7.2 When Competing Against Buildertrend**

Prospect profile: Residential GC who tried Buildertrend and hit its
limits --- doing more commercial work, has more complex subs, or needs
trade depth.

-   Buildertrend was built for residential remodel --- ask if their
    current projects fit that mold. If they\'re doing commercial TI,
    mixed-use, or multi-trade residential, Buildertrend is holding them
    back.

-   Ask about their sub relationships --- Buildertrend gives subs a
    portal, not a platform. Their subs have no job costing, no
    independent dashboard, no financial management.

-   Buildertrend has no electrical or plumbing module --- phases are
    tracked as generic to-do items.

-   Our pricing is comparable to Buildertrend\'s upper tier --- but we
    deliver significantly more depth.

**7.3 When Competing Against eSUB**

Prospect profile: Trade contractor (electrical, plumbing) currently
using eSUB who is growing into prime work, or who works with GCs and
wants both sides of the relationship managed.

-   eSUB is sub-only. If they ever win a prime contract, they need a
    second system. We replace both.

-   Cross-tenant collaboration: their GC clients can connect with them
    directly --- shared schedule visibility, shared inspection results,
    real-time invoice approvals. eSUB has none of this.

-   Our electrical and plumbing modules match eSUB\'s depth in the areas
    that matter for field work.

-   Acknowledge eSUB\'s T&M billing strength if relevant --- then show
    our T&M billing flow.

**8. Language Support --- Competitive Gap**

Spanish language support is a significant competitive gap in the
construction software market. Despite 31% of the US construction
workforce being Hispanic/Latino, none of the major platforms offer
native, first-class Spanish support across their full product. This is a
material competitive advantage at launch.

