> need the platform to work.

**8.2 Language Support as a Sales Differentiator**

In the target geographies --- Texas, California, Florida, Northeast ---
Spanish language support is not a niche feature. It is a requirements
checkbox for any contractor with field crews. Sales points by region:

-   Texas (834K Hispanic construction workers): \'Your crews can use the
    app in Spanish on day one --- no training required in their second
    language\'

-   California (808K Hispanic workers): \'Clock-in, daily reports, and
    inspection results all in Spanish --- your foremen don\'t need an
    English middleman\'

-   Florida (317K + large Haitian Creole population): \'Spanish and
    Haitian Creole (v1.1) --- covering your full workforce\'

-   Northeast (Brazilian Portuguese heavy): \'Portuguese support in v1.1
    --- tell your Brazilian crews it\'s coming\'

-   Any market: \'OSHA multilingual safety requirement --- our safety
    notifications go out in your workers\' language. That\'s your
    liability protection.\'
